// Failed authentication attempts
//
// Catches failed su and login attempts. A single failed "su - root" produces
// two distinct log lines for the same event:
//   1. "FAILED SU (to root) ..."                    from the su process
//   2. "pam_unix(su-l:auth): authentication failure" from the PAM stack
//
// Both are kept here so nothing is missed. If this were wired to an alert
// rule, dedupe on a time window per user to avoid firing twice per attempt.

Syslog
| where SyslogMessage has_any ("authentication failure", "FAILED", "Failed password")
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, ProcessName, SyslogMessage
| order by TimeGenerated desc
